@title Real-time quote pricing model
@subtitle ML Platform, Orchard Insurance, reviewed 2026-10-12
@date 2026-10-12

## Overview

The service prices about 450 quotes per second at peak, with a p99 target of 250 ms.

## Architecture diagram

diagram price dir=LR title="Quote pricing"

price: portal "Agent Portal" user
price: api "API Gateway" lb
price: lambda "Inference Lambda" fn
price: endpoint "SageMaker Endpoint" svc
price: cache "Feature Cache" cache
price: bucket "Model Bucket" store
price: pipe "Training Pipeline" svc
price: registry "Model Registry" store
price: group vpc "Inference VPC" lambda, endpoint, cache
price: group prod "Prod account" api, bucket, vpc
price: group ml "ML account" pipe, registry
price: portal -> api : quote request
price: api -> lambda : invoke
price: lambda -> cache : get features
price: lambda -> endpoint : predict
price: pipe -> registry : register model
price: registry -> bucket : approved artifact
price: bucket -> endpoint : load model

## Capacity

table = Component,Size,Scaling; SageMaker Endpoint,ml.c6i.2xlarge,4 to 12 instances on invocations per instance; Inference Lambda,1024 MB,200 reserved concurrency; Feature Cache,cache.r7g.large,2 replicas

## Deployment

1. Register the model.
2. Approve it in Model Registry.
3. Blue/green deploy, shifting 10% of traffic every 5 minutes.
4. Roll back automatically if p99 exceeds 250 ms.

!! The Feature Cache is not a source of truth. A cache miss falls back to the policy database and adds about 90 ms.
